---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
import LangSwitch from '../../../components/LangSwitch.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms of use of the Pétanque Meet app | Ludiven Studio"
	description="General terms of use of the Pétanque Meet app: account, published games and tournaments, rules of conduct, moderation, liability."
	lang="en"
	alternates={{ fr: '/petanque-meet/cgu/', en: '/en/petanque-meet/cgu/' }}
>
	<div class="wrapper stack gap-12 legal">
		<div class="stack gap-8">
			<LangSwitch lang="en" links={[{ lang: 'fr', href: '/petanque-meet/cgu/' }]} />
			<Hero
				title="Terms of use — Pétanque Meet"
				tagline="Real games, real first names, respect."
			/>
		</div>

		<p class="updated">
			<strong>Pétanque Meet</strong> app (<code>com.ludivenstudio.petanquemeet</code>) and the website's
			meet-up map — last updated: 4 November 2026.
		</p>
		<p class="updated">
			This is a courtesy translation. In case of discrepancy, the
			<a href="/petanque-meet/cgu/" hreflang="fr">original French version</a> prevails.
		</p>

		<div class="summary">
			<p><strong>Key points before you play:</strong></p>
			<ul>
				<li>The app is <strong>free</strong>, with no purchases. An advertising banner funds its running.</li>
				<li>What you publish is <strong>public</strong>. Only put in it what you agree to show everyone.</li>
				<li>Games are organised <strong>by the players, not by us</strong>. We do not guarantee that a game takes place, nor who will come.</li>
				<li>A fake, offensive or commercial listing is removed, and its account may be suspended.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>1. Purpose and acceptance</h2>
			<p>
				These terms govern the use of the Pétanque Meet mobile app and of the meet-up map of the
				ludiven-studio.fr website (together, "the Service"). By creating an account or publishing on the map,
				you accept them. If you refuse them, do not use the Service.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>2. Publisher</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Company name: <strong>Ludiven Studio</strong></li>
				<li>Legal form: EURL (French single-member limited company) with share capital of €1,000</li>
				<li>Registration: 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586 R.C.S. Vienne — SIRET 999&nbsp;253&nbsp;586&nbsp;00013</li>
				<li>Registered office: 1166 route de la Ranche, 38440 Châtonnay, France</li>
				<li>Publication director: Ludiven Studio</li>
				<li>Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a></li>
			</ul>
			<p>See also the <a href="/mentions-legales/">legal notice</a> (in French).</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>3. The Service</h2>
			<p>
				Pétanque Meet is a map of pétanque games. A player publishes a game there (a pitch, a time, the number
				of players they are looking for), and other players sign up for it. A club or an association can also
				announce a tournament there.
			</p>
			<p>
				The Service puts players in touch, nothing more. Ludiven Studio does not organise the games or the
				tournaments, does not attend them, and is not a party to the agreements between players.
			</p>
			<p>
				The Service is <strong>free</strong>. The map covers the whole world: its tiles come from the BKG, the
				German Federal Agency for Cartography (TopPlusOpen, © BKG, licence dl-de/by-2-0), with data from
				OpenStreetMap. The app shows an advertising banner served by Unity LevelPlay (ironSource Ads and Unity
				Ads), Google AdMob up to version 0.1.6: the data it uses is described in the
				<a href="/en/petanque-meet/confidentialite/">privacy policy</a> (§9).
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>4. Account</h2>
			<p>
				Looking at the map needs no account. To publish, sign up or report, you sign in with Google or Apple.
				The Service is meant for people aged <strong>15 and over</strong>; a minor must have their parents'
				consent.
			</p>
			<p>
				You are responsible for what is published from your account. One account per person: creating
				accounts to get around a limit or a suspension is forbidden.
			</p>
			<p>
				You can delete your account at any time, in the app: "Account and help" → "Delete my account". What is
				erased is described in the <a href="/en/petanque-meet/confidentialite/">privacy policy</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>5. Rules of conduct</h2>
			<p>By using the Service, you agree to:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>publish real games</strong> that you intend to play, and cancel them if you can no longer come;</li>
				<li><strong>come when you sign up</strong>, or withdraw in time;</li>
				<li>use your <strong>real first name</strong> or a nickname, never someone else's;</li>
				<li>publish nothing offensive, hateful, discriminatory, sexual or illegal;</li>
				<li>not publish a third party's personal data (name, phone number, address) without their consent;</li>
				<li>not advertise or solicit: only tournaments announced by their club or their organiser are allowed;</li>
				<li>place the pin on a place where people can play, and not at a private home;</li>
				<li>not disrupt the Service: bots, mass posting, getting around the limits, false reports.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>6. Tournaments</h2>
			<p>
				Announcing a tournament is reserved for its club, its association or its organiser. Whoever announces
				it guarantees that the information (date, place, fee, category) is accurate and updates it if it
				changes or is cancelled.
			</p>
			<p>
				The phone number and the poster are optional and become <strong>public</strong>. By sending a poster,
				you guarantee that you have the right to distribute it, including for the photos and logos it
				contains, and you authorise Ludiven Studio to show it in the Service until it is erased. Each poster is
				checked by the publisher before it becomes visible, and may be refused without justification.
			</p>
			<p>
				The entry fee is paid directly to the organiser. Ludiven Studio collects nothing and is not responsible
				for how the tournament runs.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>7. Reports, moderation and penalties</h2>
			<p>
				Anyone can report a listing or a player who did not show up. Texts go through an automatic filter, and
				a listing reported by several players is hidden pending a check.
			</p>
			<p>
				The publisher may, without notice, remove a listing, a sign-up or a poster that does not comply with
				these terms, and <strong>suspend an account</strong>: for a serious breach, or in the event of repeated
				breaches (fake games, no-shows, abuse of reporting). To challenge a decision, write to
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>.
			</p>
			<p>
				To report illegal content, use the listing's "Report" button or write to us. We deal with it as soon
				as possible.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>8. Meeting other players</h2>
			<p>
				Games bring together people who often do not know each other. Ludiven Studio does not check players'
				identity and cannot guarantee their behaviour. A few good habits:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>meet on a public pitch, at times when there are people around;</li>
				<li>tell someone close to you where you are going;</li>
				<li>report any inappropriate behaviour, and in case of danger, call 17 or 112.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Each player remains responsible for their actions, their travel and their equipment. A dispute between
				players is settled between them.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>9. Intellectual property</h2>
			<p>
				The app, its code, its interfaces, its texts and its graphics belong to Ludiven Studio. They are
				protected by intellectual property law. You receive a personal, non-exclusive right of use. The map
				tiles belong to the BKG and to the OpenStreetMap contributors, and place names come from OpenStreetMap
				(© OpenStreetMap contributors). "Pétanque" is a generic term: the Service is not affiliated with any
				federation.
			</p>
			<p>
				You remain the owner of what you publish. You authorise Ludiven Studio to show it in the Service, on
				the map and in share links, as long as the listing is online.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>10. Changes to and discontinuation of the Service</h2>
			<p>
				The publisher may change the Service, add or remove features, and change the limits (number of games
				online, of sign-ups per day…). It may suspend it for maintenance, or stop it for good. In that case,
				it will tell users in the app with reasonable notice.
			</p>
			<p>
				These terms may change. The date of the update appears at the top of the page. In the event of a
				significant change, the app will let you know; continuing to use it means you accept them.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>11. Liability</h2>
			<p>
				The Service is provided as is and free of charge. The publisher does not guarantee that it works
				without interruption, nor that the listings are accurate, up to date or honoured. It is not liable for
				the content published by users, which it removes as soon as it becomes aware of it if it is illegal.
				The ads are chosen and provided by ironSource Ads, Unity Ads and the buyers in their auctions (Google up
				to version 0.1.6): the publisher does not control their content and is not liable for the products or
				services they present.
			</p>
			<p>
				The publisher can only be held liable in the event of proven fault, and its liability is limited to
				direct damage. It does not cover a wasted journey, a cancelled game, a changed tournament or a dispute
				between players. Nothing here excludes its liability in the event of gross negligence or physical
				injury, nor limits your mandatory consumer rights.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>12. Personal data</h2>
			<p>
				The processing of your data is described in the
				<a href="/en/petanque-meet/confidentialite/">Pétanque Meet privacy policy</a>, which forms part of these
				terms.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>13. Governing law and disputes</h2>
			<p>
				These terms are governed by <strong>French law</strong>. If you are a consumer living in another member
				state of the European Union, you keep the mandatory protections of your country.
			</p>
			{/* TODO legal: replace with the mediator's name, address and website once adhesion is signed (art. L612-1). */}
			<p>
				If there is a problem, write to us first: we will look for an amicable solution. If there is no
				solution within one month, you can turn to a consumer mediator free of charge (Article L612-1 of the
				French Consumer Code). The mediator's contact details are given on request at
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>. Failing agreement, the
				dispute will be brought before the competent courts.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>14. Contact</h2>
			<p>
				For any question or to report a problem:
				<a href="mailto:contact@ludiven-studio.fr">contact@ludiven-studio.fr</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.legal {
		max-width: 68ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
		color: var(--sc-ink-2);
		font-size: var(--text-md);
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.legal h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--sc-ink);
	}
	.legal ul {
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.35rem;
	}
	.legal a {
		color: var(--sc-link);
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}
	.legal a:hover,
	.legal a:focus {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}
	.updated {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--sc-muted);
	}
	.summary {
		border: 1px solid var(--sc-line);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--sc-accent);
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: var(--sc-surface);
	}
	.summary p {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	code {
		font-size: 0.9em;
		background: var(--sc-surface);
		padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
		border-radius: 0.25em;
	}
</style>
